{
  "items": [
    {
      "description": "There are dozens of \"awesome computer vision\" repositories on GitHub. Most are encyclopedic with thousands of links arranged by topic, with no guidance on where to start, what order to read things in, or why one resource matters more than another. They are useful as archives. They are less useful as learning tools.\nThis list is built around a different idea: curation over comprehensiveness.\nEvery entry is here because it genuinely helps someone understand computer vision more deeply — not simply because it exists. Resources are organised to reflect how the field is actually learned: from image fundamentals and classical methods, through deep learning, to the transformer-era models that define current research.",
      "items": [],
      "title": "Why this list exists"
    },
